 "obiettivi": [
  "Definire la matrice di trasmissione inversa",
  "Convertire $Z\\to T$",
  "Usare ibride e trasmissione per la cascata"
 ],
 "teoria": [
  "<strong>Matrice di trasmissione inversa</strong> (ABCD): $\\begin{pmatrix}v_1\\\\i_1\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}A&B\\\\C&D\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}v_2\\\\-i_2\\end{pmatrix}$. Da $Z$: $A=\\dfrac{z_{11}}{z_{21}}$, $B=\\dfrac{\\Delta_z}{z_{21}}$, $C=\\dfrac{1}{z_{21}}$, $D=\\dfrac{z_{22}}{z_{21}}$ con $\\Delta_z=z_{11}z_{22}-z_{12}z_{21}$. Rete reciproca: $AD-BC=1$.",
  "<strong>Ibride</strong> $h$: $v_1=h_{11}i_1+h_{12}v_2$, $i_2=h_{21}i_1+h_{22}v_2$ (tipiche dei transistor)."
 ],
 "figure": [],
 "dimostrazioni": [
  {
   "titolo": "Da $Z$ alla matrice di trasmissione",
   "passi": [
    "Da $v_2=z_{21}i_1+z_{22}i_2$: $i_1=\\dfrac{v_2-z_{22}i_2}{z_{21}}=\\dfrac1{z_{21}}v_2+\\dfrac{z_{22}}{z_{21}}(-i_2)$: $C=1/z_{21}$, $D=z_{22}/z_{21}$.",
    "Sostituendo in $v_1=z_{11}i_1+z_{12}i_2$: $v_1=\\dfrac{z_{11}}{z_{21}}v_2+\\left(\\dfrac{z_{11}z_{22}}{z_{21}}-z_{12}\\right)(-i_2)$.",
    "Quindi $A=z_{11}/z_{21}$ e $B=\\Delta_z/z_{21}$. $\\square$"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "esempi": [
